.isError() and .registers[0]) are structurally built around.
    - Achieving TCP behavior with minimalmodbus would require a third-party extension/bridge not part of the core library, which is outside what a call-site 
wrapper can supply.
    - A true migration would require rewriting ModbusIO's connection management and error handling (try/except instead of isError() checks) rather than just 
swapping the client construction call, which goes beyond what a glue-code wrapper at the identified call site can achieve.

